executionContract.intendedBehavior:
Change what a QA seat does when the landed gate misses. Today every miss exits the seat. After this change, a QA seat in a worktree-mode control checkout (HEAD on moe/control) handles a claimed REVIEW row whose recorded completion is not a landed commit it can review like this:
- It parks only that row: one moe.report_blocked (blockedOnTaskIds []), a [WARN] MOE_CONTROL_CHECKOUT_BEHIND line, and no CLI.
- It then goes back to its loop top for a fresh pre-flight and claim, still registered. This holds even under --no-loop / -NoLoop.
Only seat-level conditions still stop the seat with exit 1, exactly as worktree_stop / Stop-MoeWorktreeSeat do today:
- no context for this task;
- an unreadable control HEAD;
- a git error in the ancestry check;
- a completion miss while the control HEAD lacks the target tip the pre-flight synced;
- a report_blocked that fails.

